# Code owners — Boston AI Atlas
#
# Today the atlas has one maintainer, so everything routes to @holzerjm. That makes
# review requests automatic; it does not by itself block anything. A code-owner review
# is only REQUIRED once a ruleset on `main` turns on "Require review from Code Owners"
# (docs/repo-transfer.md, step 7) — and do not turn that on while this file names a
# single person: GitHub never counts an author's approval of their own PR, and the
# ruleset has no bypass list, so the only maintainer could no longer merge anything.
#
# Planned two-person rule, once a second owner exists (e.g. a team in the TOA org with
# at least two members, replacing @holzerjm below):
#   - Entries that carry `affiliation` in data.js (the publisher and its sponsors) and
#     the narrative files — the STAGES founder tips in data.js, user-facing copy in
#     index.html, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, MAINTAINING.md, docs/ — are approved by
#     someone other than the person who wrote the change, so no one person can reword
#     the publisher's or a sponsor's entry alone (docs/independence-policy-draft.md).
#   - CODEOWNERS matches files, not lines, so it cannot single out the affiliated entries
#     inside data.js. Assigning data.js to the team means every maintainer-authored
#     data.js change gets a second reviewer; community PRs are unaffected in practice
#     (the author is not a maintainer, so one maintainer approval is already a second
#     person). If that proves too heavy for routine rota updates, narrow it with a CI
#     check that flags PRs touching an affiliated entry, instead of dropping the rule.
#   - .github/ (workflows and this file) stays with the owners team, so the rule
#     cannot be edited away by the same person it constrains.
#
# Syntax: the last matching pattern wins; owners need write access to the repo, or
# the line is ignored (https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners).

*                           @holzerjm

